				<td align="left" class="TextMain">
					<center><h2>Rules And Conduct For GPK</h2></center>

					What are GPKs?<BR><BR>GPK's are in-guild currency used for the »purchasing« of 
					loot that drops on guild run raids. As the abbreviation » guild particiaption 
					kredits« hints these are gained by taking part on guild raids or other events 
					including helping fellow guildies obtaining their epics. This system is used to 
					promote guild participation and to elliminate so called bad lottos, that is 
					items being won by players that have no real use for them.<BR><BR>How are GPKs 
					obtained?<BR><BR>GPKs are awarded for participating in guild raids or other 
					events. Each encounter is valued separately based upon the difficulty of the mob 
					and several other factors. You can see the value of each individual encounter in 
					the » enccounter chart«. The values there are prone to change when some 
					encounters get trivial for us or we target new mobs to kill or the encounters 
					listed are found harder that the amount of allocated GPKs hint. GPKs are only 
					given for encounters listed in encounter chart. Other events may also be given 
					GPK status and value if Garaddor peronally approves it. Raid leaders of GPK 
					raids are expected to keep track of the people who have attended raid and how 
					many GPKs they have earned during that raid. Players are requested to inform 
					raid leaders of their time of arrival and time of departure on and from that 
					raid. Raid leader is then expected to post the amount of GPKs earned by each 
					individual on the appropriate section of our website. There is a chart on our 
					website displaying the amount of GPK that each member poseses and is updated 
					daily. GPKs are given to players not to characters or accounts meaning even if 
					you have 5 accounts and play with 4 characters simultaneously you get the amount 
					of GPKs another player with one account and one character would get. In the 
					event of a auction tie (2 or more playes offer the exact same amount of GPKs for 
					an item and none wish to increase the price) a /ran 100 takes place and the 
					winner pays the highest auctioned price. <BR><BR>How are GPKs used to aquire 
					items?<BR><BR>Items are distributed by means of an auction where GPKs are used 
					as currency. The class that can use the item »their class name is listed on the 
					item« and is on the raid »has been in a fight to kil lthe mob« can enter the 
					auction. The player offering most GPKs for the item loots the item. It is 
					allowed to auction on items useable by characters other than the one you are 
					currently being on a raid with provided that you have stated that you would like 
					to auction on that characters loot before the start of the raid and that other 
					character is OVER lvl 50. Items that cannot be used by anyone on raid or noone 
					bids on them are saved in ADD guildbank and are on auction for main characters 
					only for 3 days after the raid. After those 3 days are up the items are on 
					auction for any character (including lvl 1 twinks if anyone wishes) for another 
					3 days. Items that are not wanted even then are kept by guild to be sold in 
					market to finance cleric gems and wizard portstones. Armor quest gems that drop 
					during raid are saved in ADD guildbank and are given freely to anyone in guild 
					that has obtained required piece of armor and has high enough faction. If loot 
					drops that only one person on raid can use then no auction takes place and the 
					plazer that will use that item pays a set amount of Gpk for it even if it pushes 
					his account into negative.<BR><BR>The amount of GPKs each person can use on a 
					specific raid is the amoun of GPK that person had at the start of that day. That 
					means if the person had 120 GPK at start of day and has been on 2 raid earning 
					additional 25 GPKs he/she can still only use 120 GPKs on the eventual 3rd raid. 
					GPKs earned during that raid day will not be taken into account until next 
					day.<BR><BR>Epic items that drop are given for the price of 1 gpk to players 
					with most GPK points present on raid.<BR><BR><BR><BR>What happens if out of 
					guild people/friends join the raids?<BR><BR>In that case the person rolls agains 
					everyone in our guild that can and will use the item. If that peron wins the 
					roll he naturally loots the item. If that person/persons lose the roll then 
					auction takes place as if the other people were not on raid. <BR><BR><BR>Who can 
					participate in auctions?<BR><BR>Items are auctioned on by players who can use 
					the item (their class/race is listed on the item) and they have positive number 
					of GPKs (their account is not in negative figures). If noone on raid can use the 
					item it goes to guildbank and is treated as described 
					above.<BR><BR><BR>Exceptions to auction system!<BR><BR>Exceptions to auction 
					system arise when it is clear that an individual has »earned« a specific item. 
					»Earning« would mean that an individual has spent large amounts of time waiting 
					for the mob to pop and is instrumental in reserving that mob until a sucessfull 
					kill by ADD. Example would be camping Lodizal for long periods of time with 
					intent to obtain map piece or shell used in shield quest. The person must state 
					well before the mob pops which item he/she is after. If that item does not drop 
					when the mob is killed the auction takes place as if there were no special 
					circumstances. If that item does drop though the person pays a preset amount of 
					GPKs and loots it withought auction taking place on that specific item. <BR>					

					<br>GPKs are only taken into account if at least 2 full groups are on the raid.<BR>

					<BR><BR><br>
				</td>
